  "issue": {
    "body": "Following https://github.com/tiangolo/fastapi/issues/791: \r\n\r\nIt seems starlette is not routing URL with encoded slash in it.\r\n\r\n## To Reproduce : \r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom starlette.testclient import TestClient\r\n\r\nfrom starlette.applications import Starlette\r\nfrom starlette.responses import JSONResponse\r\nfrom starlette.routing import Route\r\n\r\n\r\nasync def get_unit(request):\r\n    unit = request.path_params[\"unit\"]\r\n    return JSONResponse({\"unit\": unit})\r\n\r\n\r\nroutes = [Route(\"/units/{unit}\", endpoint=get_unit)]\r\n\r\napp = Starlette(debug=True, routes=routes)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef test_base():\r\n    client = TestClient(app)\r\n    response = client.get(\"/units/kg\")\r\n    assert response.json() == {\"unit\": \"kg\"}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef test_encoded_char():\r\n    client = TestClient(app)\r\n    response = client.get(\"/units/kg%c2%b2\")\r\n    assert response.json() == {\"unit\": \"kg\u00b2\"}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef test_encoded_slash():\r\n    client = TestClient(app)\r\n    response = client.get(\"/units/kg%2fs\")\r\n    assert response.json() == {\"unit\": \"kg/s\"}\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\ntest_encoded_slash is not working.\r\n\r\n## Expected behavior\r\n\r\nStarlette is routing the request and retuning the expected json.\r\n\r\n## Environment\r\n\r\n* OS : Windows 10\r\n* Starlette version : 0.13.1\r\n* Python 3.7.3\r\n\r\n## Additional context\r\n\r\nStarlette regexp seems fine after inspecting the app routes : `app.routes[0].path_regex` : \r\n\r\n`'^/units/(?P<unit>[^/]+)$'`\r\n\r\n```python\r\n>>> import re\r\n>>> pattern=re.compile('^/units/(?P<unit>[^/]+)$')\r\n>>> pattern.match('/units/kg%2Fs')\r\n<re.Match object; span=(0, 13), match='/units/kg%2Fs'>\r\n>>> pattern.match('/units/kg%2Fs').groupdict()[\"unit\"]\r\n'kg%2Fs'\r\n```",
    "closed_at": "2022-02-14T10:28:05Z",
    "created_at": "2020-02-13T20:27:33Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/826",
    "number": 826,
    "state": "closed",
    "title": "[BUG] Routing of encoded slash URL",
    "user": "jules-ch"
  },
